Design Document: Personal Finance & Expense Manager
1. Design Philosophy
The interface follows a "Dark-Centric Professional" theme. The goal is to make financial data feel less like a spreadsheet and more like an intelligent command center.

Intelligence: Use high-contrast accents to highlight insights.

Simplicity: Minimalist borders and generous whitespace (negative space) to prevent data fatigue.

Style: A sophisticated palette that conveys security and modern fintech vibes.

2. Visual Style Guide
2.1 Color Palette
Inspired by the Moneta aesthetic, the application utilizes a deep-space background with vibrant neon highlights.

Primary Background: #010103 (Deep Obsidian) – Provides a high-end, sleek foundation.

Surface/Card Color: #0F0F12 – Slightly lighter than the background to create depth through layering.

Primary Accent: #3A41B2 to #1A1999 (Electric Violet/Indigo Gradient) – Used for primary buttons, active states, and branding elements.

Success/Income: #00C896 (Mint Green) – For positive cash flow and budget-safe indicators.

Warning/Expense: #FF4C61 (Soft Coral) – For expenditures and budget alerts.

Typography: #DEE1E5 (Off-White) for headings; #9B9AA2 (Slate Gray) for secondary body text.

2.2 Typography
Headings: Sans-serif (e.g., Inter or Montserrat), Semi-bold. Focused on readability at large scales for dashboard totals.

Body/Data: Monospaced-leaning sans-serif (e.g., JetBrains Mono or Roboto Mono) for numerical values to ensure perfect vertical alignment in transaction lists.

3. UI Components & Layout
3.1 The "Glassmorphism" Dashboard
The main interface features floating "cards" with subtle borders.

The Hero Stat: A large, centered display of the "Total Monthly Spend" using a gradient text effect.

Insight Cards: Compact modules showing "Highest Spending Category" and "Remaining Budget" using circular progress rings.

Glass Effect: Cards should have a subtle 1px border (rgba(222, 225, 229, 0.1)) and a slight backdrop-blur to create a premium feel.

3.2 Interaction Design
Hover States: Buttons should utilize a soft outer glow (drop-shadow) in the primary accent color when hovered.

Empty States: When no transactions exist, use a minimalist SVG illustration with the indigo accent color to guide the user to "Add First Expense."

Transitions: Smooth 0.3s ease-in-out transitions for opening modals or switching between monthly views.

4. Key Screens & Elements
4.1 Global Sidebar / Navigation
A slim, vertical sidebar on the left.

Icons: Simple, linear stroke icons (2px weight).

Active State: A vertical indigo pill-shaped indicator next to the active menu item.

4.2 Transaction List
Moving away from standard tables to a "Activity Feed" style.

Iconography: Each category (Food, Tech, Rent) has a unique, circular-masked icon.

Typography Hierarchy: Transaction Name (Bold/White) over Date (Small/Gray), with the Amount aligned to the far right.

4.3 Data Visualization
The Moneta Chart: A custom-styled Doughnut chart for category breakdown.

Palette: Instead of a rainbow of colors, use varying shades of the primary Indigo and Violet to maintain a cohesive brand look.

5. Mobile Responsiveness
Stacking Logic: On mobile, the Sidebar collapses into a bottom navigation bar.

Touch Targets: All actionable elements (buttons, list items) maintain a minimum height of 48px for ease of use.

Condensed Dashboard: The Hero Stat remains prominent, but secondary insight cards scroll horizontally.